1. Functional Requirements
 Prompt Input Interface: The system must provide a user-friendly input field where users can enter a story concept, genre, characters, or theme.
 Gemini Model Integration: The application must securely connect with Google Gemini APIs to process user prompts and generate creative responses.
 Structured Script Generation: The output must be organized into clear comic book structures, including page numbers, panel layouts, visual descriptions, and character dialogues.
 Export Functionality: Users should be able to view, copy, or download the generated comic script for further production.
2. Non-Functional Requirements
 Performance: The AI generation response time should be optimized to deliver script outlines within a few seconds.
 Usability: The user interface must be intuitive, clean, and responsive for seamless navigation.
 Reliability: Proper error handling must be implemented to manage API rate limits or connection failures gracefully.
 Security: API keys for the Gemini models must be stored securely using environment variables (⁠.env⁠) rather than hardcoded into the source code.
3. Hardware Requirements
 Developer Workstation: PC or Laptop with minimum 4GB RAM, stable internet connection, and a modern web browser.
 Server/Deployment (Optional): Cloud hosting environment (such as Streamlit Cloud, Render, or Vercel) with internet access to call external APIs.
4. Software & Technology Requirements
 Programming Language: Python 3.8+
 AI/ML SDK: Google GenAI SDK (⁠google-generativeai⁠)
 Framework (UI/App): Streamlit or Flask (depending on your build)
 Version Control: Git and GitHub for phase-wise repository management
